  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "If $A={a,b}$ and $B={1,2},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times A\\times B?$\n\n- $(a,a,1)$\n- $(b,a,2)$\n- $((a,b),2)$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and the third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${a,b}$ with ${a,b}$ and ${1,2},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\times A\\times B={ & (a,a,1),(a,a,2),(a,b,1),(a,b,2), \\\\  & (b,a,1),(b,a,2),(b,b,1),(b,b,2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|A\\times A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(a,a,1)$ and $(b,a,2)$ are in $A\\times A\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
